feat(cli): make /refresh re-read everything it can

Three things can change underneath a running agent: the configuration, the skill
roots, and an MCP server that failed to start. They were three commands, and
`/refresh` did one of them, which is not what a person means by the word.

`/refresh` now does all three. `/reload` stays as an alias so a habit keeps
working, and the two spellings are asserted to parse to the same command rather
than to look alike by accident.

The retry touches only the servers that failed: one that is connected keeps its
process and its session, so refreshing cannot disturb it. A server that fails
again keeps its place with the new reason, and the command says how many are
still unreachable.

The retry runs without holding the servers lock across an await, which would
have blocked the runtime; the lock is taken once, to install the result.
